# VS Code REST Client (`humao.rest-client`). Run `auth.http` first — every request here needs an
# Access Token, and the `@token` variable below is where you paste it.
# The three upload requests need real files: point the `< ./path` lines at any small image.
# The rules these requests demonstrate are proven end to end by:
#   npm run verify:profile
#   npm run verify:completed-work
#   npm run verify:media

@host = http://localhost:3000/api
@token = PASTE_AN_ACCESS_TOKEN

### My Profile — 200. One payload for both profile screens.
# @name me
GET {{host}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### No token — 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{host}}/users/me

### Edit Profile — 200. Only the listed fields exist; anything else in the body is dropped.
PATCH {{host}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "נינה",
  "lastName": "לוי",
  "bio": "עשרים שנות ניסיון בקידוח יסודות.",
  "specialties": ["drilling", "concrete"],
  "businessPhone": "052-1234567",
  "city": "תל אביב",
  "region": "tel_aviv",
  "travelRadiusKm": 60,
  "delayToleranceDays": 3,
  "noticeRequiredDays": 2
}

### Clearing an optional value — 200. `null` clears; leaving the key out changes nothing.
PATCH {{host}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "businessPhone": null }

### Smuggled fields — 200, and every one of them is ignored.
PATCH {{host}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "נינה",
  "email": "attacker@example.com",
  "status": "banned",
  "profileComplete": true,
  "companyName": "Hijacked Ltd",
  "availability": "closed",
  "passwordHash": "x"
}

### Empty patch — 400 REQUEST_VALIDATION_FAILED
PATCH {{host}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Out of range — 400 REQUEST_VALIDATION_FAILED
PATCH {{host}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "travelRadiusKm": 5000 }

### `other` without its free text — 400 REQUEST_VALIDATION_FAILED
PATCH {{host}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "specialties": ["other"] }

### Company fields — 200. Company name, office phone and availability belong to the company,
### so they are edited here and only by a member holding `company.manage`.
PATCH {{host}}/companies/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "לוי עבודות חשמל בע\"מ", "officePhone": "03-1234567", "availability": "limited" }

### Without that permission — 403 COMPANY_PERMISSION_DENIED
### With no active membership at all — 403 NO_ACTIVE_COMPANY

### Completed Work — 201. No `onFieldSync` key exists in the contract: the badge is derived
### by the server, so a client cannot claim it.
# @name workEntry
POST {{host}}/users/me/work-entries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "מגדל הראשונים",
  "scope": "קידוח יסודות ודיפון",
  "meta": "2025 · תל אביב"
}

### Completed Work with a photo — 201. Multipart, one file under `image`.
POST {{host}}/users/me/work-entries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=FieldSyncBoundary

--FieldSyncBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

מגדל הראשונים
--FieldSyncBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="meta"

2025 · תל אביב
--FieldSyncBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="site.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./site.png
--FieldSyncBoundary--

### A link to work the server cannot verify — 422 WORK_LINK_NOT_VERIFIABLE.
### Projects and tasks arrive in Stage 3; until then no link can be proved, so none is accepted.
POST {{host}}/users/me/work-entries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Linked", "meta": "2025", "projectId": "000000000000000000000000" }

### Remove a Completed Work item — 204. Its photo goes with it.
DELETE {{host}}/users/me/work-entries/{{workEntry.response.body.entry.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Somebody else's entry — 404 WORK_ENTRY_NOT_FOUND. A wrong owner and a wrong id answer alike.
DELETE {{host}}/users/me/work-entries/000000000000000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Avatar — 200. JPEG, PNG or WebP, up to 5 MB, streamed straight into GridFS.
PUT {{host}}/users/me/avatar
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=FieldSyncBoundary

--FieldSyncBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="avatar"; filename="avatar.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./avatar.png
--FieldSyncBoundary--

### Anything else — 400 UNSUPPORTED_FILE_TYPE. The declared MIME type is checked, not the name.
### Over 5 MB — 413 FILE_TOO_LARGE. A wrong field name — 400 UNEXPECTED_FILE_FIELD.

### Remove the avatar — 200, and the stored file is deleted.
DELETE {{host}}/users/me/avatar
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Serve an image — 200. The path comes from `avatarUrl` / `imageUrl`; it is never a storage path.
GET {{host}}/users/me/assets/PASTE_AN_ASSET_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Somebody else's asset — 404 FILE_NOT_AVAILABLE. Knowing an id is not authorization.
GET {{host}}/users/me/assets/000000000000000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
